In article <PETTERI.95May30145830@halli.meridian.fi>, petteri@halli.meridian.fi (Petteri Soikkonen) writes:
|>Hello,
|>
|>is there somewhere GNU Emacs mode for using decladebug 
|>same way like with gdb or dbx?


Put the following line in your ~/.emacs file:

(load-file "/usr/opt/LDB406/emacs/lisp/decladebug.el")

Then, to start it, M-x decladebug

You will get a minibuffer like:

Run DECladebug like this: decladebug <type your arguments here>

And you're off and running.  There are limitations with the up and down
commands not moving the source window.  They have been fixed and will be
released with the next major release of DECladebug (December-ish).

You must have GNU Emacs 19.22 or higher.

Regards,
Tim

