Connecting Macintosh or PC (those with SCSI connections) external CD-ROM
drives to an OSF Alpha seems (currently!) to require that drive to use 512
byte buffers for its data transfer.  With CD-ROMs of today this is a problem
since a lot of them use a data buffer length of 2048 bytes.  The standard
DEC supplied drivers (special files) only support such hardware that use I/O
buffers of 512 byte length.

I for one want to use Macintosh and PC CD-ROMs on an OSF1 (version 3.0b)
Alpha 200 4/166.  But in so doing, I do not wish to reinvent the wheel.

Thus my question of two part:
1.  is there available a device driver which will work under OSF1 that will
      support these longer buffers? 
2.  which of the various manufacturer's models of external CD-ROMs
      available today have been successfully used with OSF Alphas? 
      
I am sure others would like to know the answers to these questions just as I
am confident that somewhere out there on the net someone knows the answers?

