A few words of warning:

resolv+ uses an older copy of bind as it's base, and will have any and
all bugs associated with that release of bind.  As far as I know, it
has never been ported to a more recent release of bind (4.9.3BETA17
is the current release - see http://www.isc.org/).

Installing resolv+ is no different than updating the shared C library to
do DNS only, so take your pick as to which way you want to go.  resolv+
gives you some of the capability of /etc/svc.conf in that you can specify
how to do hostname lookups.


