The only way is to install OSF 2.0 first (as an upgrade) and than 3.2.
Be warned !!! We did a reinstallation from 1.2 to 3.0 four weeks ago and
now there are tons of problems we never had before :^(( So I suggest that 
you try the way across 2.0. A few things to remark:

1. Make a full (!!!) backup of your system hd. You cant imagine what things
   you need to remember after a reinstallation ...
2. If you have more than one machine to update - install one and try out all
   your favorite utilities - than make the others ready.
3. If you aren't an expert of OSF and UNIX in general I recomment that you 
   make use of a person who has done such reinstallation before.
4. Don't make the installation during a time in which you propably need the
   machine for business.

To see what could happen here are some of our problems after complete 
reinstallation (machine was DECAlpha 3000 series 500)

- some X-applications were not installed (cdaviewer, dxnotepad, ...)
- man-pages are an option now - be careful with the install script
- some c-include files were not found (even stdio.h - mysterious ...)
- shared-libraries were not fully complete installed
- many problems with NIS (server side)
- wonderful things happen when adding new users (perhaps a NIS problem)

...as a result almost nothing worked correctly after the installation so
we did a lot by hand. Now after a couple of weeks the system is nearly stable.

		Hope that helps - Cheerio, Bernd.
