In article <3pmm1m$9ou@lantana.singnet.com.sg> koonteck@merlion.singnet.com.sg (Chua Koon Teck) writes:

ctk> Hi I am having problem adding a user account into the NIS
ctk> master server.  I have tried using the XSysAdmin to add a
ctk> user account into the NIS map but when I tried to su or
ctk> login to the user account, it report Unknown id error.  I
ctk> have also tried the manual way of adding an entry into the
ctk> /var/yp/src/passwd file but encounter the same error.

I seem to recall that XSysAdmin in v3.2 as shipped did not
automatically update the NIS map from the map source file.
Try this:

	cd /var/yp
	make prpasswd passwd group

If that's not enough, you'll probably find that it added the user
into the /etc/passwd file (and possibly /etc/group) rather than
/var/yp/src/passwd and /var/yp/src/group.  Move the data to map
source files in /var/yp/src and rebuild the maps.

[mailed *and* posted]

