Harry> space but it was running out of INODES (or is it VNODES with
Harry> AdvFS)

Harry> I found nothing obvious in the manuals, anyone know how to
Harry> increase the number of files I can have on an AdvFS disk ?

The problem is that Advfs isn't expressly designed for having tons of
small files on it such as a News partition.  If you are running OSF
3.2 or higher, you can use the undocumented -x option for mkfdmn.  You
want something like this:

	mkfdmn -x X /dev/rz#c news

to make a news domain with lots of preallocated Metadata cells, where
X is some arbitrary number, such as 50000 or even 250000, but I
haven't tries this to any great extent.  Hope this helps.

Also, a good place to find information on stuff like this is the
Alpha-OSF-managers archive, which can be searched via the web.  The
URL is:

	http://www-archive.stanford.edu/lists/mlists.html

