X-Deja-AN: 103111489
organization: The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill
newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1


: Have succesfully compiled rz and sz. Would please anyone tell me in
: detail the required steps to dial and run this programs via a to port
: 1 connected modem? (How to set up the terminal spec. files, how to set the
: baud-rates, the handshake-protocols, how to set the AT-commands in the modem,
: etc, etc.)
X-Newsreader: TIN [version 1.2 PL2]

Here are the steps I used.I have a supra faxmodem v.34 attached to the serial
port of my alpha 3000-600 using a straight-thru 25 wire cable.

First, I used kermit (kermit -l /dev/tty00 -b 38400) to set my modem
parameters) I have a supra modem and I used AT&F2S0=1.

Second, modify /etc/inittab to tell it to spawn a getty. I used:
tty0:23:respawn:/usr/sbin/getty tty00 M38400 vt100
You will want to use M2400 for your modem.
I used a straight through cable to my modem. It has hardware flow
control, and the AT&F2 sets things up so that it responds to DCD and DTR.
To tell init to reread the inittab, use
init q
If you do a ps ax you should see a getty spawned and connected to /dev/tty00.


