:    Therefore, I need to install "netmsgserver". To install "netmsgserver" it is
: necessary install "mach_init" and that it is runned as the first process (see the
: details in "Mach 3 Server Writer's Interfaces", appendix C, Service Server, page
: 149). I suppose that people writing servers and clients for Mach3 had to do
: something similar. I don't know to install "mach_init" for it is runned as the
: first process (before /sbin/init). Can somebody tell me how to install "mach_init"
: and "netmsgserver" ? (I don't have experience installing Mach servers).

To get 'netmsgserver' running, the easiest way is to change the nanny 
configuration file: (/usr/etc/nanny.config, as under Mach 2.6 MSD)
netmsgserver {
RUNFILE=( )
SCRIPT=( /usr/etc/netmsgserver)
UID=( msgsrv)
GID=( network)
NICE=( 0)
ATTRIBUTES=( mach)
}

This gets the server running and checks whether it keeps running.

