> I have a problem with a LAT printer under OSF1.
[...] 
> Then i have added in my /etc/printcap
> # Printer HP
> HP2LASER|lp4|4:\
>         :br#19200:\
>         :ct=dev:\
>         :fc#0177777:\
>         :fs#023:\
>         :lf=/usr/adm/lp4err:\
>         :lp=/dev/tty0e:\
>         :mx#0:\
>         :of=/usr/lbin/lpf:\
>         :pl#66:\
>         :pw#80:\
>         :sd=/usr/spool/lpd4:\        
>         :xc#0177777:\
>         :xf=/usr/lbin/xf:\
>         :xs#044000:
>[...] 
>         waiting for HP2LASER to become ready (offline ?)
> 
> The printer is online (obviously) and the same printer is 
> configured in another VMS host and work perfectly.

I see some possible causes:

- did you try the hplaserof filter? (usr/lbin/hplaserof as if and of
  parameter in /etc/printcap)

- is tty0e defined (latsetup)?

- is the respawn parameter of the tty0e getty entry in /etc/inittab changed
  to off? Should look like
  lat0e:3:off:/usr/sbin/getty     /dev/tty0e      console vt100
  (if you change it online, execute the command "init q" afterwards)

- is your (obviously correct) latcp command executed at reboot?
  If not, insert it in /sbin/init.d/lat, or better: create a separate
  /sbin/init.d/latsetup file and call it from an appropriate /sbin/rc3.d
  entry (i.e. S59latsetup)

- is the XON/XOFF flow control enabled on the printer AND the terminal 
  server?


hope this helps,
Eric



