> Has anyone gotten Crack_4.1 (or any version of crack) to run on OSF version >
> 3.0?
> 
> When trying to run Crack (which makes itself - no makefile is used), I keep
> getting the following compiler errors:
> 
> /usr/lib/cmplrs/cc/cfe: Error: crack-fcrypt.c, line 254: Syntax Error
            Ll ^= (S0L)[ *dp STEP];
        ---------------------^

I succeeded in getting Crack V4.1f running on my OSF/1 V3.2 system earlier
this week.  To get it to compile, you need to fix bytesex.c as follows:
	diff bytesex.c.org bytesex.c
	6c6
	<     long int l;
	---
	>     int l;
	19d18
	<       l <<= 32;
Replacing the long int by an int and eliminating the left shift
statement fixes the broken logic for determining endianism on a 64-bit
machine.

To get it to run without core dumping, you need to add a #include statement
to crack-supp.c:
	diff crack-supp.c.org crack-supp.c
	10a11
	> #include <time.h>

Good Luck,

Ram Rao
Digital, Indianapolis




