organization: Network/development platform support, NMTI
newsgroups: comp.infosystems.www.users,comp.infosystems.www.browsers.misc,comp.unix.questions,comp.unix.osf.osf1

This sounds like standard "terminal isn't in raw mode" behaviour. A really
icky workaround is to override lynx by wrapping it in a script:

	stty -echo cbreak; /real/path/to/lynx; stty echo -cbreak

When you built lynx, did you tell it you had a System V or BSD system?
OSF/1 behaved much more like a BSD than a System V system. I'm running
lynx on OSF/1 3.2 right now with no difficulty.
