Eric> Does AdvfsCacheMaxPercent already exist on OSF/1 2.0 and is it
Eric> also set to 7% by default? Is it recommendeded to lower
Eric> UBCMaxPercent if AdvfsCacheMaxPercent is set to a higher value?

I don't know about the first question, but you should be able to check
this out with the command:

	sysconfig -q advfs

And see what it says.  Of course this could be a 3.x only program, so
what you would probably have to do is look through the kernel while
it's running with dbx.  I'm almost positive that the name will be
different though.

UBCMaxPercent just sets the maximum amount of RAM the UBC can use,
what normally happens is that UBC and VM fight it out and it seems to
stay fairly balanced.  But most of my tuning experience is under 3.2
and 3.2a, so I can't comment on OSF 2.0 or earlier.

John




