> Just setup our new OSF/1 system (ver 3.0). Have OSF-BASE, OSF-USR Paks
> put in. Yet there are times when it responds 'Too many users login,
> try again later' for new logins even though there are only 3 users 
> using the system. 
> I checked that the kernel have 64 users defined, and the /dev/ttyp*
> are more than enough. So i use lmf to view the registered Paks

Yup, this has nothing to do with it.


> using subcommand list, I can see that the field Users:Total for all other Paks
> are 'unlimited' except OSF-USR which says 2
> What is the meaning of this field ? I use 'list full for OSF-USR' to
> view the detailed ifo, but found nothing about this '2' thing.
> Has this got anything to do with this problem of 'too many users'
> false message or I have to look for something else.

I think you will find that OSF3.0 has the weird habit of creating its own
OSF-USR unless it finds one already when it registers OSF-BASE.  It calls it
OSF-IMPLICIT-USR or something like that and it allows only 2 users.  It also
overrides the setting in any OSF-USR you register later.  I have been hit by
this before.

The solution is to lmf issue the implicit license and then reset to make
sure that the valid OSF-USR is being read.


Ciao,							Marco
