In <3otrje$l2e@aragorn.unibe.ch> willers@butp.unibe.ch (Moritz Willers) writes:
>Only f77 on the DEC gives the following:
>
>itpalpha (~/dec) 3 % f77 -o dumy dumy.f incl.f
>Assertion failed: 0, file
../../../../../../src/usr/ccs/lib/libmld/cmrlc_produce.c,  
>line 864
>Fatal error in: /usr/lib/cmplrs/cc/ld IOT/Abort trap 

An official patch is in the works for this.  In the mean time, try linking
with -O1, like this:

	% f77 -c dumy.f
	% f77 -c incl.f
	% f77 -O1 -o dumy dumy.o incl.o

You need only perform the link step at -O1, you may still compile at
higher optimization levels.

