In article <Pine.ULT.3.91.950425150224.1515S-100000@jerry.alf.dec.com>,
Jimeee Womack  <womack@jerry.alf.dec.com> wrote:
>		Does anyone know why the size of quota.user
>	is so large?? The default  size of quota.user would seem
>	to be 2097120. It looks like the file is sparse, but I cannot
>	find any info that explains why this file is so large, I only 

quota files are indeed sparse, and the size of the file is determined
by the maximum UID used (I don't know what it count as used).

2097120/32 corresponds to UID 65534 (65535 records since it allocates
one record for root/0), which should be the user 'nobody'. 

'root' acesses on NFS-mounted filesystems are often mapped to this
UID, so it might be that the filesystem has been NFS exported to
another host, and root has looked/modified (I'm not sure what is
required) something from a client.



