In a world where supposedly everyone is making the switch to GUI
interfaces, in three good Motif engines, one of the things people
mention about their systems are their *character based* admin tools :-)

I've used all three. They're all OK, they all have their flaws. I prefer
the USG sysadm/FMLI look-and-feel, but SMIT's ability to show you the
actual Unix command line being built from your menu choices is a big
