One error I've seen is STORAGE.DLL not knowing about >2GB of disk space,
and therefore giving a "not enough disk space" error when trying to
save a document to a file system with >2GB of free disk space.

This is a Microsoft problem, not a Digital one. If this is what you
are seeing, contact Microsoft.  A workaround is to create a large file
to bring the free space below 2GB.

