liq@next1.msci.memst.edu (qian li (Grad)) writes:

>I have been looking for SLIP or PPP for OSF/1 for a while but couldn't get
>it.  I wonder is there any of you out there running SLIP or PPP on your OSF/1?
>If yes, could you tell me where I can get it or which version would be the
>easiest one to port from.


Digital Unix (and DEC OSF/1) comes with slip as part of the os. It works
fine. 'ppp' has also been adapted to DEC OSF/1 , but because it uses the
insertion of streams modules and the serial ports are clist , you need to
force the use of the streams by doing an rlogin to yourself. I have done
this also.  I was running Netblaser/slip to Alpha/slip and also Ultrix/ppp
to OSF/ppp. The former is much easier.

