How do you propose to run CGIs without a server?

What we need is browsers that will open a named socket.  Then your admin tool
binds to that socket and serves HTTP when it needs to.  Using the named socket,
you aren't exposed to the net, right?  Of course, you have to make sure that
the permissions on the socket won't let just anyone open it and gate it to
the net. 

Of course, there are the remote-control mechanisms, but they tend to be very
browser-specific.  AFAIK, they still require a net connection, too.




