I have thought about this, some.

You can use the same basic technique that Satan does, with a custom server
that swizzles the password in the request path. In fact, you can make the
request path an encrypted password that is changed on every transaction, so
that even if you snoop it and start using it you'll be blown very quickly when
the server software stops working for the authorized user.

Of course with this mechanism you won't be able to use the "BACK" command from
your client.
