In Article <1995May8.170003@sdg.dra.com>
sean@sdg.dra.com (Sean Donelan) writes:
>Is there a trick to making traceroute use source routing?  I've gotten
>a couple of versions of traceroute off the net, and looked at comer's
>book and code.  But something inside DEC OSF/1 (Digital Unix) seems
>to munge the option header.

This is actually a BSD Reno netetwork code problem and is not specific to
Digital UNIX. I found a note from Stevens describing the problem in some
detail, but basically it resolves to:
You set the IP options to specify a loose source route. You then set the TTL
to 1. Unfortunately the code to do raw socet options wipe out any IP options,
so it does not work. You cna force the TTL or you can set IP options, but not
both.

I would love to see Digital fix this. It's a major hassle to log into a SunOS
system somewhere to do lstraceroute.

