For recording and playing back audio, you need Multimedia Services for
DEC OSF/1 (last release before it switches to Digital UNIX).  If your system
came with Digital UNIX (ne'e OSF/1) installed, it should have Multimedia
Services as well.  Look for the following subsets:


MMEMANRT150                     Multimedia Services for OSF/1 Man Pages for Runtime V1.5
MMEMSB150                       Microsoft Sound Board Device Driver V1.5
MMERELNOTES150                  Multimedia Services for OSF/1 Release Notes V1.5
MMERT150                        Multimedia Services for OSF/1 Runtime V1.5
MMERTSMPLDAT150                 Multimedia Services for OSF/1 Sample Audio and Video Data V1.5

If your system didn't come with factory installed software, you should have
at least gotten the PAK for this product with your system and you can find
the software on the Layered Products CD.

For a CD player, look at /usr/examples/motif/xcd.  There's a nice public
domain player available at ftp://ftp.x.org/contrib/applications/xmcd

