jcampbel@csn.org (John Campbel) wrote:
>I'm new to this OSF/Unix stuff, but i need some help configuring my >Internet server as a DNS server.  I want to be able to have pe=
ople send >mail to my server using user@domain.org instead having to supply the >fully qualified host name.  What do I need to put i=
n my hosts.db and >hosts.rev file.  I don't have any other hosts on my network to handle >mail.  All users get the mail on the Inter=
net Server.

First:  
Post messages like this to comp.protocols.tcpip.domains, or info.bind
Not here.

Second: 
It's the FQDN (Fully Qualified Domain Name) that you don't want to type 
in, there's no such thing as a FQ host Name.

Third:
Add a MX record to your hosts.db file to include a reference to your 
domain.  eg
mydomain.uk  IN  MX  10 host1.mydomain.uk
mydomain.uk  IN  MX  10 host2.mydomain.uk

Fourth:
Get a copy of DNS and BIND. (ISBN 1-562592-010-4, Albitz & Liu, 1993) 
It's not perfect, but does answer questions like yours.

Hope this helps!
Tom Cooper




