In article 3mk@encomix.com, dune@encomix.com (David Deza) writes:
>I'm  going to install Windows NT  in a DEC Alpha 2000-500 running
>OSF/1,  I have read the manual but  I think the guys of Microsoft
>don't  speak  my  language (of course  they  speak  english and I
>don't).  So  I will thank all  the information you could send me,
>I'm  specially interested in how to set  up a disk, a whole disk,
>to  receive  Windows  NT  and prepare  a  boot  menu  to use both
>operating system (OSF/1 and Windows NT).

I wanted to do the same thing on my DEC Alpha 2000-300 that I could have
choosed at boot time with which OS I want to work. 
After talking to Digital Support Switzerland, I decided not to install the
Win NT as second OS. DEC sayd that the NT scans the disks quite heavy and puts
a kind of a 'stamp' on disks which FS can not be read by the NT. Like this, the 
disks with the OSF/1 becomes corrupt.
They said that the only way to have both OS on the same machine is, that you 
unconnect the disks with the OS where you dont need at this time. For this,
you have to have externel SCSI disks, if you dont want to open the cover
of the Alpha every time.

Hope this helps a bit

greetings

Reto
