tgr@omega.csuohio.edu (Wayne A. Hogue II) writes:

>Does anyone have a set of patches to allow WUftp to work with C2 security
>enabled?

>thanks,

>-Wayne

The following change should do the trick:

in src/config/config.osf add the lines

#define SecureWare
#include <sys/types.h>
#include <sys/security.h>
#include <prot.h>
#define crypt(a,b) bigcrypt(a,b)

SCO UNIX's security interface is almost identical to OSF's it seems - just
the bigcrypt call in this case. If it works, but users cannot log in,
then manualy replace any 'crypt' calls with 'bigcrypt' calls.
