Why do you wan't an other way isn't one enough?  If what you mean is 
that you want to find out without actually (re)booting the system 
then use:

uerf -R -r 300

This lists startup event information (record class 300) which is all 
the stuff that comes up on the screen when you boot including 
physical memory.

