In <3odjps$231@homer.alpha.net> Mark Palmer <palmer> writes:

>Does anyone know of a command that will tell how much real memory is 
>installed under OSF/1 v3.0
>
Use vmstat and compute (act + free + wire) * 8192.  The result will be
only a few megs less than the amount of real memory installed.  If you
have top installed, you can avoid the computation by looking at its
output.

If you want the exact value, compile this proggie:

    #define ULT_BIN_COMPAT 1
    #include <stdio.h>
    #include <sys/sysinfo.h>

    main()
    {
	int memsize;

	getsysinfo(GSI_PHYSMEM, &memsize, sizeof(memsize), NULL, NULL);
	printf("This machine has %d Kb of memory\n", memsize);
	return 0;
    }

The #define is needed for OSF/1 2.x.

Dan
