Crude, but this is what I did...

Edit /etc/remote and make an entry for your modem. I just duplicated
the entry for dialer9600 and bumped the baud rate up to something 
reasonable. I then "tip dialerxxx", or whatever I called the /etc/remote 
entry. You'll get a connect. Then ATDT-dial to where you want to go.
Once you get a connection, go to another window and type something like
"slattach +e tty00 19200"

This assumes that you setup a slip interface and so forth in the setup 
script for network interfaces.

BTW, this is what I'm waiting for....

ppp that runs on OSF which autoredials whenever the connection is 
dropped. Anyone got something magical like that? I don't even think 
anyone has pppd running on osf yet.

greg





