In article <danpop.799707629@rscernix> danpop@afsmail.cern.ch (Dan Pop) writes:
>>uerf -R -r 300
>>
>The problem is that those messages lie about the physical memory.
>
>                                        physical memory = 62.00 megabytes. 
>                                        available memory = 54.00 megabytes. 
>
>Needless to say, I don't have 62 megs of physical memory on my system,
>but 64.  Anybody knows where the missing 2 megs have been lost?

They don't lie. You have 64 Mbytes of memory installed in your machine
physically, but when OSF got there, only 62 Mbyte where still left. The
remaining 2 Mbyte are claimed by the console code and PAL code. From OSF
perspective, the rest doesn't exist. In the future, this 2 Mbyte penalty
will become smaller due to better sharing of memory and other optimizations.

