I'm not sure anybody actually answered this.  The released version of
UPS (2.45.2) does not support the Alpha, but the new, gdb-based
version does.

To build from source, you need:

	ups-3.7-alpha.tar.Z
	   found at 	unix.hensa.ac.uk:/misc/unix/ups

	gdb-4.13.tar.gz
	   found at    ftp.uu.net/other GNU archive site

	perl-4.036.tar.gz
	   found at    ftp.uu.net/many archive sites

You also need GNU zip to uncompress the .gz files.

I have successfully built these with the DEC cc compiler, so I don't
think that gcc is needed, but it should work also.  Note that "alpha"
here means "alpha-test", and this version definitely has some bugs in
it, but it does seem to be working well enough to be useful.
