organization: Digital Equipment Corporation
reply-to: werme@zk3.dec.com
newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1

eckman@eos1.larc.nasa.gov (Richard Eckman) writes:

>  Since upgrading to Digital UNIX v3.2, I've noticed that a number of
>our DEC 3000/400's have exhibited UBC write errors with the following
>form:

>UBC write error(4) on device (0,0) at block 0 size 8192

>  Could someone tell me what these errors mean?

UBC: Unified Buffer Cache
error(4): EINTR
device (0, 0): Generally means NFS, unfortunately.

These generally mean that a NFS write failed (often involving a crashed server).
The intent was to report disk errors better, but NFS confuses things because
it often retries failed writes.  I believe that V3.4 will not print these for
NFS, or at least tame them quite a bit.
