   I noticed that the Makefile for the kernel has the
   flags -g3 and some defines having to do with profiling,
   can I obtain a kernel which doesn't have this stuff in it,
   but which is fully functional?

If you look in the config file for your kernel, you'll see a
couple of 'makeoptions' lines. One of them adds debugging info
to the kernel, the other adds profiling info (methinks). 

Anyway, I commented them both out and added

makeoptions	LDOPTS="-x"

and it seems to work just fine. My kernel's about 4MB.

For grins, I'll post my config file. Your mileage may
vary---DON'T USE IT unless you understand it REALLY well.
If anyone else out there has suggestions for trimming it
down in any significant fashion, I'd love to hear it.

Mike

