thanks for the reply.  I'm going to summarize some of the
responses I got from people:

1) no, stripping the kernel will NOT reduce the RAM usage.
It WILL break ps and related programs.

2)  using 'makeoptions LDOPTS="-x"'  (maybe mispelled?)
reduced the disk image of the kernel to about 1/2 without
breaking anything.  This strips out local debugging info
but not global symbol information, according to the manpage.

3) removing options you don't need DOES reduce the RAM usage.
However, you can't go very far in this direction.  (All the
DEC people who wrote me remarked on this.)

4) reducing maxusers also seemed to reduce RAM usage:  mine
was 32 and is now 16.  I'm not sure how much this really helps.

Thanks to all who have responded.

Regards,

